  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency protection-based assistance for older women and men, including older people with disabilities in Dnipropetrovska and Kharkivska Oblasts in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This program builds on ongoing BHA funded project and previous grants to provide psychosocial support (PSS) to older people affected by the conflict through a case management approach of Home-Based Care (HBC), Community Safe Space (CSS) activities, and provision of individualized protection assistance. This integrated protection intervention will ensure that older people who face mobility restrictions, are isolated or are adopting negative coping mechanisms, have improved access to humanitarian aid and social services, and are re-integrated into their communities in order to  and improve their psychosocial wellbeing and resilience. 
Additionally, HelpAge will provide technical capacity building and mentoring to of selected NGOs and government departments on , in age and disability -inclusive programming to meet the &#x2018;Humanitarian Inclusion Standards on Older People and People with Disabilities&apos;, and inclusive case management and HBC standards adapted to the Ukrainian context. Given the existing vulnerabilities and protection concerns faced by older people, including those with disabilities, in Eastern Ukraine, HelpAge will complement direct protection assistance with advocacy at the local and national levels to ensure that older people&apos;s diverse concerns and vulnerabilities are addressed.
The project will support: 
(i) vulnerable older people  through a case-management approach of home-based care (HBC and), psychosocial support (PSS,) including those with reduced mobility, who will be supported through peer to peerpeer-to-peer activity and, referrals. They will also receive , as well as some  who will be provided with hygiene kits, adult diapers/incontinence pads and appropriate assistive products; 
(ii) older people through peer recreational activities , awareness raising, skill building and social inclusion activities at Community Safe Spaces. This, includesing the creation of older people Peer Champions and Initiative Groups who will benefit from  capacity building on older people&apos;s issues, community mobilisation and sustainable community support; and 
(iii) HelpAge staff and staff from humanitarian and development agencies to build their capacity in Humanitarian Inclusion Standards, case management approach, HBC, PSS and advocating for older people&apos;s rightsissues.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To improve the security, dignity and wellbeing of the older women and men, including older people with disabilities, affected by the ongoing conflict in Eastern Ukraine through access to inclusive, protection-based humanitarian support at individual household and community level.</narrative>
  </description>
